{
  "id": "tse-01-03",
  "slug": "simplifying-any-linear-expression",
  "title": "Simplifying Any Linear Expression",
  "courseId": "two-step-equations",
  "chapterId": "ch1-distributing-and-combining-with-rational-coefficients",
  "minutes": 10,
  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "c1",
      "kind": "concept",
      "figure": "sign-rule-table",
      "body": "You now have every tool for simplifying linear expressions: distribute using the sign rule, then combine like terms using the signed-number rules."
    },
    {
      "id": "i1",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Distribute, then combine.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "algebraTiles",
        "prompt": "Build 3(x + 2) + 4x with tiles — open the group first, then bring in the 4x. Set the x-count and the constant to what you are holding.",
        "targetX": 7,
        "targetConst": 6,
        "maxTiles": 8,
        "xStart": 0,
        "constStart": 0,
        "successFeedback": "7x + 6. Opening 3(x + 2) put 3 x-tiles and 6 units on the table; the 4x joined the x-tiles and nothing joined the units.",
        "xFeedback": "Check the x-tiles. Three come out of the brackets and four arrive from the 4x — they are the same kind of tile, so they stack together.",
        "constFeedback": "Check the units. Three copies of 2 make 6, and the 4x has no units to contribute — an x-tile and a unit tile are different objects and never combine."
      },
      "predict": {
        "prompt": "In 3(x + 2) + 4x, can the 4x combine with anything BEFORE distributing?",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "notyet",
            "label": "Not yet — the 3x is locked in the parentheses"
          },
          {
            "id": "two",
            "label": "Yes — with the 2"
          },
          {
            "id": "three",
            "label": "Yes — with the 3"
          }
        ],
        "outcomeId": "notyet",
        "reveal": "The parentheses hide a 3x that only distribution releases — until then the 4x has no visible partner. The 2 inside is no partner either: an x-term can only combine with another x-term, never with a bare number. Unlock first, then collect."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "k1",
      "kind": "check",
      "body": "A negative multiplier version.",
      "conceptTag": "tse-simplify-mixed",
      "explanationVariants": [
        "-2(x+3)=-2x-6, then -2x+6x=4x, giving 4x-6.",
        "Distribute first, then combine the x-terms."
      ],
      "widget": {
        "type": "buildExpression",
        "prompt": "Simplify: -2(x + 3) + 6x",
        "tokens": [
          {
            "id": "t0",
            "label": "4x"
          },
          {
            "id": "t1",
            "label": "-"
          },
          {
            "id": "t2",
            "label": "6"
          },
          {
            "id": "t3",
            "label": "+"
          },
          {
            "id": "t4",
            "label": "8x"
          }
        ],
        "correct": [
          "t0",
          "t1",
          "t2"
        ],
        "acceptAlso": [],
        "commonBuilds": [
          {
            "sequence": [
              "t0",
              "t3",
              "t2"
            ],
            "feedback": "-2 times 3 is -6, not +6: -2(x+3)=-2x-6."
          },
          {
            "sequence": [
              "t4",
              "t1",
              "t2"
            ],
            "feedback": "Combine ONLY the x-terms: -2x+6x=4x, not 8x."
          }
        ],
        "reusable": false,
        "missFeedback": "Distribute first (sign and all), then combine the x-terms and the constants separately.",
        "successFeedback": "Yes — -2(x+3)=-2x-6, then -2x+6x=4x, giving 4x-6."
      },
      "variant": {
        "gen": "g7-tse-expression-build",
        "form": "tseMixedPlus"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c2",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "The order of operations always matters: distribute (multiply into the parentheses) before you combine (add matching terms together).",
      "figure": "tse-simplify-order"
    },
    {
      "id": "i2",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Pure combining, no distribution.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "mcq",
        "prompt": "Simplify: -4x + 9x",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "label": "5x",
            "correct": true,
            "feedback": "Yes — different signs: 9-4=5, keep positive (9 is bigger): 5x."
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "label": "-5x",
            "feedback": "9 has the bigger magnitude and is positive, so the result is positive: 5x."
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "label": "13x",
            "feedback": "Different signs means subtract, not add: 9-4=5, so 5x."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c3",
      "kind": "concept",
      "body": "Practice noticing which pattern you're facing — pure distribution, pure combining, or both together — before you start computing.",
      "figure": "tse-simplify-order"
    },
    {
      "id": "i3",
      "kind": "interactive",
      "body": "Pure distribution, no combining.",
      "widget": {
        "type": "mcq",
        "prompt": "Distribute: -4(x + 3)",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "a",
            "label": "-4x - 12",
            "correct": true,
            "feedback": "Yes — -4 times x is -4x, and -4 times 3 is -12."
          },
          {
            "id": "b",
            "label": "-4x + 12",
            "feedback": "-4 times 3 is -12, not +12."
          },
          {
            "id": "c",
            "label": "4x - 12",
            "feedback": "The x-term keeps the -4's sign too: -4x, not 4x."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "k2",
      "kind": "check",
      "body": "Distribute and combine, another mix.",
      "conceptTag": "tse-simplify-mixed",
      "explanationVariants": [
        "4(x-2)=4x-8, then 4x-6x=-2x, giving -2x-8.",
        "Distribute first, then combine the x-terms."
      ],
      "widget": {
        "type": "buildExpression",
        "prompt": "Simplify: 4(x - 2) - 6x",
        "tokens": [
          {
            "id": "t0",
            "label": "-2x"
          },
          {
            "id": "t1",
            "label": "-"
          },
          {
            "id": "t2",
            "label": "8"
          },
          {
            "id": "t3",
            "label": "+"
          },
          {
            "id": "t4",
            "label": "10x"
          }
        ],
        "correct": [
          "t0",
          "t1",
          "t2"
        ],
        "acceptAlso": [],
        "commonBuilds": [
          {
            "sequence": [
              "t0",
              "t3",
              "t2"
            ],
            "feedback": "4 times -2 is -8, not +8: 4(x-2)=4x-8."
          },
          {
            "sequence": [
              "t4",
              "t1",
              "t2"
            ],
            "feedback": "Combine correctly: 4x-6x=-2x, not 10x (that adds instead of combining signed coefficients)."
          }
        ],
        "reusable": false,
        "missFeedback": "Distribute first (sign and all), then combine the x-terms and the constants separately.",
        "successFeedback": "Yes — 4(x-2)=4x-8, then 4x-6x=-2x, giving -2x-8."
      },
      "variant": {
        "gen": "g7-tse-expression-build",
        "form": "tseMixedMinus"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "k3",
      "kind": "check",
      "body": "Pure combining, negative result.",
      "conceptTag": "tse-simplify-mixed",
      "explanationVariants": [
        "Same signs: 6+8=14, keep negative: -14x.",
        "Both negative coefficients add and keep the sign."
      ],
      "widget": {
        "type": "buildExpression",
        "prompt": "Simplify: -6x - 8x",
        "tokens": [
          {
            "id": "t0",
            "label": "-"
          },
          {
            "id": "t1",
            "label": "14"
          },
          {
            "id": "t2",
            "label": "x"
          },
          {
            "id": "t3",
            "label": "2"
          }
        ],
        "correct": [
          "t0",
          "t1",
          "t2"
        ],
        "acceptAlso": [],
        "commonBuilds": [
          {
            "sequence": [
              "t1",
              "t2"
            ],
            "feedback": "Both coefficients are negative, so the sum stays negative: -14x."
          },
          {
            "sequence": [
              "t0",
              "t3",
              "t2"
            ],
            "feedback": "Same sign means add, not subtract: 6+8=14, so -14x."
          }
        ],
        "reusable": false,
        "missFeedback": "Distribute first (sign and all), then combine the x-terms and the constants separately.",
        "successFeedback": "Yes — same signs: 6+8=14, keep negative: -14x."
      },
      "variant": {
        "gen": "g7-tse-expression-build",
        "form": "tseMixedSameNeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "ch1",
      "kind": "challenge",
      "body": "The trickiest one yet.",
      "conceptTag": "tse-simplify-mixed",
      "explanationVariants": [
        "-5(x-3)=-5x+15, then -5x+2x=-3x, giving -3x+15.",
        "Distribute first (watch the double-negative), then combine."
      ],
      "widget": {
        "type": "buildExpression",
        "prompt": "Simplify: -5(x - 3) + 2x",
        "tokens": [
          {
            "id": "t0",
