        "form": "tseMixedChallenge"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r1",
      "kind": "recap",
      "body": "Distribute using the sign rule, then combine like terms using the signed-number rules — in that order.",
      "takeaways": [
        "Distribute before combining, always.",
        "Use the sign rule (same=positive, different=negative) at every step.",
        "Practice spotting which pattern you're facing before computing."
      ],
      "teaser": "next chapter: running distribution backwards — pulling out a common factor, then choosing the form that answers the question."
    }
  ],
